{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"16907fe07c4bb266d28d66d5996b9f9dfe9a0d925dbb68ba0e09c89b36b5cb0d","digest":{"component_or_area":"test fixtures / rebar repo template","key_entities":["_rebar_repo_template","tests/interfaces/conftest.py","rebar.list_tickets()","rebar.init_repo()","pytest.MonkeyPatch.context()","tests/interfaces/test_rebar_repo_isolation.py::test_template_stays_virgin"],"problem_keywords":["fixture assertion","template initialization","test invariant enforcement","ticket store isolation"],"propositions":["The template fixture _rebar_repo_template must assert the freshly built template contains no tickets, inside the MonkeyPatch context where REBAR_ROOT and cwd are pinned.","Test-level checks in test_template_stays_virgin only protect narrowed pytest runs that select that test; fixture-level assertions are needed to protect all consumers regardless of test selection.","The no-tickets assertion must fire at construction time before any test runs, not only when a specific test is selected, to prevent silent inversion of downstream assertions that depend on template emptiness."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787333443614938001,"uuid":"e2a05995-641d-45b8-bb21-22b778af58b3"}